00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:23.680
Right.

223
00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.120
But they last under one month

224
00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.600
and then the person returns to normal,

225
00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.320
that's brief psychotic disorder.

226
00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.160
Correct.

227
00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.640
Then if it lasts between one and six months,

228
00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.120
it's schizophrenia form disorder.

229
00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.080
And if it crosses that six month mark,

230
00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.560
it becomes schizophrenia.

231
00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:37.720
What is magically happening at month six?

232
00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.160
It's not magic, it's neurobiology and prognosis.

233
00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.160
Okay, how so?

234
00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.520
Well, the brain can experience brief psychotic breaks

235
00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:48.120
due to immense acute stress or trauma.

236
00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.440
Like a person might completely detach from reality

237
00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.800
for two weeks under severe duress.

238
00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.360
Just totally break from reality.

239
00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.840
Yes, but once the stressor resolves,

240
00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.880
their brain returns to baseline.

241
00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:00.880
That's a temporary malfunction.

242
00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.440
But as those symptoms stretch past six months,

243
00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:04.600
we're no longer looking

244
00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.760
at a temporary stress induced break.

245
00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.120
What are we looking at then?

246
00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.600
We're looking at an insidious,

247
00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.520
pervasive neural cognitive change.

248
00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:15.520
The six month threshold is the boundary

249
00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.240
where clinicians have to recognize

250
00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.200
that this is a lifelong management issue,

251
00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.560
not just a passing storm.

252
00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.960
Okay, that makes sense.

253
00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.600
But what about when psychosis overlaps with a mood disorder?

254
00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.400
Like when someone is deeply depressed

255
00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.120
but also having delusions,

256
00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.160
the manual gets really specific there too.

257
00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.000
It does.

258
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.840
That's where the clinician has to look very closely

259
00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.920
at the timeline again

