00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.800
Because of the physiological mechanism.

456
00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:23.920
Alcohol and sedatives

457
00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:27.040
are profound central nervous system depressants.

458
00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:29.640
Over time, the brain constantly pumps out

459
00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:31.720
excitatory chemicals just to keep you awake

460
00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:34.480
and functioning against the heavy suppression of the alcohol.

461
00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:35.300
Oh, I see.

462
00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.160
So the brain is pressing the gas pedal to the floor

463
00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.960
just to counter the breaks of the alcohol.

464
00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:39.800
Exactly.

465
00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.480
So what happens when you abruptly stop drinking?

466
00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.580
The breaks are gone.

467
00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.320
The breaks are suddenly gone.

468
00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:47.280
But the brain is still flooring the gas pedal.

469
00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:50.080
The central nervous system, essentially short circuits.

470
00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:54.000
This massive over excitation leads to severe seizures

471
00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:56.440
